  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 213 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nFriday through Tuesday:\n\nLow pressure continues to gradually fill in over the eastern Great\nLakes through Friday, leading to continued gusty north winds and a\nfew lingering wrap-around showers in the CSI region. Expect highs\nin the upper 40s. Any lingering precipitation exits Friday night,\nwith a cold airmass sinking into the western Great Lakes as high\npressure builds in. Overnight lows in the low 30s are expected\nunder clearing skies and diminishing winds. Any remaining\nsensitive vegetation should be covered or brought indoors. High\npressure continues to sink southward into the southern Plains and\nLower Mississippi Valley, allowing winds to shift to southwesterly\non Saturday. Expect highs around 50 degrees.\n\nHigh pressure lingers across the Plains and Lower Mississippi \nSunday through Monday, with multiple shortwaves moving along the \nnorthern edges of the high through the Upper Midwest. Expecting \ngenerally dry conditions to prevail, with perhaps a few passing \nshowers (~15% chances). If any shortwave becomes stronger or the \nsouthern Plains high weakens faster, some more widespread \nprecipitation may develop. High pressure begins to shift eastward \nMonday through Tuesday, bringing increasing southwesterly winds as\na stronger low propagates eastward through southern Canada. \nTemperatures are expected to remain somewhat steady through early \nnext week, with highs around 60 degrees and lows in the mid-30s.\n\nMH",
